StarFighter AMD / F2-A bring-up notes
=====================================

Base
----
- Layout: `src/mainboard/starlabs/cezanne` (`include/variants.h`, `variants/<name>/`)
- Earlier Myst-style baseboard split was dropped in favor of that layout.
- SoC family: `soc/amd/phoenix`

AMI source
----------
- `ARN39EP023`
- Project token: `OemProjectPkg/ARN39EP/ARN39EP.sdl`
- Public product naming should follow StarFighter, not the factory ARN39 ref.
- Board is wired as Phoenix FP7 / Mayan-class in the AMI tree.

Artifacts to mine next
----------------------
- Final BIOS:
  - `Build/Phoenix/RELEASE_VS2015/FV/AMIROM.fd`
  - signed output `ARN39EP.rom`
- EC blob:
  - `OemProjectPkg/ARN39EP/OemEcMirror/OemEcMirror.sdl`
- PD blobs:
  - `OemProjectPkg/ARN39EP/OemPdMirror/OemPdMirror.sdl`
- APCB:
  - `AmiAgesaWrapperPkg/AmiApcbGen/PhoenixFp7/PhoenixFp7.sdl`
- PSP/SMU/MP2/MPIO payload layout:
  - `AmiPspPkg/PspLayout/PHX/BuildPspPhx_L2A.txt`
  - `AmiPspPkg/PspLayout/PHX/BuildPspPhx_AB.txt`

Blobs layout
------------
- EC image path follows Cezanne: `3rdparty/blobs/mainboard/starlabs/starfighter_amd/starfighter/ec.bin`
  (VARIANT_DIR is `starfighter`).

Known placeholders in this skeleton
-----------------------------------
- GPIO tables are intentionally minimal.
- DXIO routing is tentative.
- DDI routing is tentative.
- Devicetree only keeps the obvious Phoenix/eSPI/EC structure.
- Silicon init uses OpenSIL (not FSP); USB PHY policy belongs in OpenSIL or
  board ramstage hooks, not FSP `mcfg->usb_phy_ptr` devicetree registers.
- Board `fw.cfg` lists PSP/amdfw blobs; adjust against the AMI PSP layout when
  validating a new binary set.
